WEBVTT

asr-000077
00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:29.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The briefing of the fiscal year 2027 proposed expenditure program of the Office of the Presidential Advisor on Peace, Reconciliation and Unity is hereby called to order.

asr-000088
00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:34.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At this juncture, the Chair recognized the Committee Secretary to acknowledge the resource persons present for today.

asr-000089
00:28:35.320 --> 00:28:38.660
Committee Secretary: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Good afternoon. Good afternoon to our resource persons.

asr-000090
00:28:38.660 --> 00:28:46.900
Committee Secretary: For the briefing on the proposed FY2027 Budget of the Office of the Presidential Advisor on Peace, Reconciliation, and Unity, or OPAPRU,

asr-000091
00:28:47.220 --> 00:28:49.020
Committee Secretary: we'd like to acknowledge our resource persons.

asr-000092
00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:54.500
Committee Secretary: From OPAPRU, we have Secretary Mel Senen Sarmiento, together with Undersecretary Wilben Mayor,

asr-000093
00:28:54.500 --> 00:29:02.140
Committee Secretary: Undersecretary Noel Baraceros, Undersecretary Jeffer Mancol, Executive Director Mary Marjorie Martin-Chan,

asr-000094
00:29:02.540 --> 00:29:08.500
Committee Secretary: Executive Director Susana Guadalupe Marquedia, Executive Director Andres Aguinaldo Jr.,

asr-000095
00:29:09.660 --> 00:29:16.620
Committee Secretary: Director Basil Castaño, Director Jenny Claire Mordeno, Director Laila Halud, Director Jana Jill Gallardo,

asr-000096
00:29:16.900 --> 00:29:20.440
Committee Secretary: Director Christina Lauren Umali, and Director Jay Anthony Peña.

asr-000097
00:29:20.440 --> 00:29:23.960
Committee Secretary: We have also invited representatives from DBM and COA.

asr-000098
00:29:24.080 --> 00:29:24.440
Committee Secretary: For DBM...

asr-000099
00:29:24.500 --> 00:29:28.900
Committee Secretary: For DBM, we have OIC Assistant Director Mary Rose Aguilar and Ms. Maricel Dizon.

asr-000100
00:29:29.240 --> 00:29:34.160
Committee Secretary: For COA, we have Mr. Ryan Jeric Balada and Mr. Romel Fabi.

asr-000101
00:29:34.320 --> 00:29:35.100
Committee Secretary: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000102
00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:36.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-000103
00:29:37.440 --> 00:29:40.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: First, the Chair would like to welcome everyone.

asr-000104
00:29:41.140 --> 00:29:44.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I'd like to give my opening statement for today's deliberation.

asr-000105
00:29:44.400 --> 00:29:51.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We will tackle the FY2027 Budget of the Office of the Presidential Advisor on Peace, Reconciliation, and Unity,

asr-000106
00:29:51.660 --> 00:29:54.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and ensure that its allocation will be efficiently spent.

asr-000107
00:29:54.500 --> 00:29:59.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Through the proper delivery of its programs towards peace and national harmony.

asr-000108
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:15.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The agency's role is highly important in maintaining the government's integrity in honoring pacts and agreements, formulating strategic and comprehensive peace programs, and cultivating dialogues that lead to conflict resolutions and trust-building.

asr-000109
00:30:15.340 --> 00:30:32.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As we take up the agency's budget, we also highlight the implementation of the agency's PAMANA program as its flagship initiative in delivering livelihood, education, and developmental support to conflict-affected areas and conflict-vulnerable communities.

asr-000110
00:30:32.500 --> 00:30:44.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa kasalukuyan, marami pang nangyayaring hidwaan sa loob at labas ng ating bansa. Marami tayong pagkakaiba, madalas, magkakasalungat ang ating paniniwala, pinanggagalingan, at paninhindigan.

asr-000111
00:30:45.340 --> 00:30:58.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ngunit sa kabila ng lahat ng ito, iisang ating layunin sa pagdinig na ito na ang pambansang pondo ay magbibigay daan sa mapayapa, tapat, at nagkakaisang serbisyo.

asr-000112
00:30:58.400 --> 00:31:08.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our national fiscal space may be limited, but we will do our best to sustain not just the country's prosperity, but also its peace and stability. Thank you very much.

asr-000113
00:31:09.720 --> 00:31:15.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I now call on Secretary Mel Senen Sarmiento to deliver his opening statement and to present the 2027

asr-000114
00:31:15.340 --> 00:31:22.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: National Expenditure Program of the Office of the Presidential Advisor on Peace, Reconciliation and Unity.

asr-000115
00:31:22.960 --> 00:31:25.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Secretary Mel, you now have the floor.

asr-000116
00:31:25.320 --> 00:31:38.440
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Thank you, Your Honor. Napakaganda po ng nasabi niyo kanina. Kapayapaan po, napakalaga para po makamit natin ang ating hinahangad na mga economic and development goals.

asr-000117
00:31:39.480 --> 00:31:44.900
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Malaking leksyon kung titignan po natin sa buong Asia ang nangyayari sa South Korea.

asr-000118
00:31:44.900 --> 00:31:51.000
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: For example, in the 50s, meron po silang internal conflict na nakapekto sa kanila.

asr-000119
00:31:52.300 --> 00:31:58.900
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: We were six times richer than South Korea per capita wise in the early 1950s.

asr-000120
00:32:00.320 --> 00:32:05.040
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Tinulungan pa po natin sila. We contributed $2 million para sa kanilang reconstruction.

asr-000121
00:32:05.040 --> 00:32:11.000
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: But since then, they were able to focus on their economic and development growth.

asr-000122
00:32:12.280 --> 00:32:14.880
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Ngayon po, kung titignan natin ng South Korea, napakalaga.

asr-000123
00:32:14.900 --> 00:32:16.740
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Napakalaki na po ng kanilang narating.

asr-000124
00:32:17.820 --> 00:32:20.160
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Ganon din po ang nangyayari sa Vietnam.

asr-000125
00:32:21.840 --> 00:32:31.040
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Natapos po yung kaguluhan doon, April 30, 1975, they were able to focus on their economic and development growth.

asr-000126
00:32:31.480 --> 00:32:35.140
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: And nahabol na po tayo nila.

asr-000127
00:32:35.880 --> 00:32:40.860
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Napakalaga po kung titignan natin ang ating posisyon.

asr-000128
00:32:40.860 --> 00:32:44.680
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Ang ating na-mention.

asr-000129
00:32:44.900 --> 00:32:45.720
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Ang ating fiscal space.

asr-000130
00:32:46.200 --> 00:32:47.460
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Ang ating balance sheet.

asr-000131
00:32:47.580 --> 00:32:50.500
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Palagi pong napekto ang pag may kaguluhan po sa ating bansa.

asr-000132
00:32:50.720 --> 00:32:54.700
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: Kaya tama po kayo, Your Honor, na napakalaga po ng kapayapaan sa ating bansa.

asr-000133
00:32:55.520 --> 00:33:02.260
OPAPRU Secretary Mel Senen S. Sarmiento: With that, I would like to request Usec Wilben Mayor to present our budget.

asr-000134
00:33:03.420 --> 00:33:05.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Usec Wilben Mayor, please.

asr-000135
00:33:06.320 --> 00:33:08.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: You now have the floor to present the budget.

asr-000136
00:33:09.120 --> 00:33:09.960
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Thank you, sir.

asr-000137
00:33:09.960 --> 00:33:12.680
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: To the chairperson, Committee on Finance.

asr-000138
00:33:13.820 --> 00:33:14.880
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Honorable Secretary.

asr-000139
00:33:14.900 --> 00:33:16.180
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Senator JV Ejercito.

asr-000140
00:33:17.080 --> 00:33:24.760
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Thank you for the opportunity and presenting the proposed budget of OPA proof for 2027.

asr-000141
00:33:27.840 --> 00:33:30.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Shown in this screen is the outline of the presentation.

asr-000142
00:33:33.980 --> 00:33:34.840
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Next slide.

asr-000143
00:33:35.520 --> 00:33:38.080
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: In the 2026 State of the Nation Address,

asr-000144
00:33:38.780 --> 00:33:42.260
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. affirmed the government's commitment

asr-000145
00:33:42.260 --> 00:33:44.880
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: to fulfilling the signed peace agreement

asr-000146
00:33:44.900 --> 00:33:47.040
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: as the President emphasized,

asr-000147
00:33:48.320 --> 00:33:52.940
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: peace must be demonstrated through actual implementation and completion.

asr-000148
00:33:53.900 --> 00:33:57.100
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: For OPA proof, this means accelerating remaining commitments

asr-000149
00:33:57.100 --> 00:34:02.840
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and working toward the substantial completion of all peace agreements by 2028.

asr-000150
00:34:04.320 --> 00:34:08.180
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: At the core of our proposal is the agency's expanded mandate.

asr-000151
00:34:08.920 --> 00:34:12.080
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Under Executive Order No. 158, Series of 2021,

asr-000152
00:34:12.080 --> 00:34:14.560
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: it reinforces our key role,

asr-000153
00:34:14.900 --> 00:34:17.440
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: in advancing a just and lasting peace for the nation,

asr-000154
00:34:17.440 --> 00:34:19.940
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: one that benefits all Filipinos,

asr-000155
00:34:19.940 --> 00:34:24.460
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: especially those in conflict-affected and vulnerable communities.

asr-000156
00:34:24.460 --> 00:34:31.000
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The agency is guided by the Five-Point Peace Reconciliation and Unity Agenda,

asr-000157
00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:35.680
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: as shown, which is the policy anchor of the different peace processes,

asr-000158
00:34:35.680 --> 00:34:38.920
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: the PAMANA, and other peace-building programs.

asr-000159
00:34:38.920 --> 00:34:44.160
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: As of September 30, 2026,

asr-000160
00:34:44.160 --> 00:34:48.500
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: we have achieved an overall accomplishment of 71%

asr-000161
00:34:48.500 --> 00:34:50.900
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: in the implementation of peace agreements.

asr-000162
00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:54.880
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: This indicates that while we have reached significant milestones,

asr-000163
00:34:55.620 --> 00:34:57.480
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: there is still substantial work ahead

asr-000164
00:34:57.480 --> 00:34:59.900
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: to fully complete our commitments.

asr-000165
00:35:01.280 --> 00:35:04.280
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: This remaining gap highlights the need to sustain momentum

asr-000166
00:35:04.280 --> 00:35:07.700
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and, more importantly, to accelerate implementation.

asr-000167
00:35:08.720 --> 00:35:10.120
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Additional funding is critical,

asr-000168
00:35:10.120 --> 00:35:13.000
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: not only to sustain ongoing initiatives,

asr-000169
00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:16.140
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: but also to catch up on delayed deliverables.

asr-000170
00:35:16.140 --> 00:35:22.260
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: With Fiscal Year 2027 as the last full year of the current administration,

asr-000171
00:35:22.260 --> 00:35:27.060
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: we must maximize this period to ensure a successful transition

asr-000172
00:35:27.060 --> 00:35:30.760
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: toward substantial completion by 2028.

asr-000173
00:35:30.760 --> 00:35:37.560
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The peace process with the Moro-Islamic Liberation Front, or MILF,

asr-000174
00:35:37.560 --> 00:35:42.460
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: has achieved 67% overall accomplishment in implementing the signed peace agreement.

asr-000175
00:35:42.460 --> 00:35:50.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: 100% in the political track, highlighted by the conclusion of the first parliamentary elections,

asr-000176
00:35:50.600 --> 00:35:53.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and 49% in the normalization track,

asr-000177
00:35:53.600 --> 00:35:57.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: with significant progress in security commitments,

asr-000178
00:35:57.600 --> 00:36:01.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: including the deployment of Joint Peace and Security Teams, or JPSTs,

asr-000179
00:36:01.600 --> 00:36:05.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: management of Small Arms and Light Weapons, or SALT-W,

asr-000180
00:36:05.600 --> 00:36:09.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and sustainment of the ceasefire and security mechanisms.

asr-000181
00:36:09.600 --> 00:36:11.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The implementation of the peace process

asr-000182
00:36:11.600 --> 00:36:16.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: with the Moro National Liberation Front, or MNLF,

asr-000183
00:36:16.740 --> 00:36:19.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: has reached 43% completion.

asr-000184
00:36:19.740 --> 00:36:24.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Its political track has completed 70% of the commitments,

asr-000185
00:36:24.740 --> 00:36:29.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: with only the establishment of the Bangsamoro Development Assistance Fund, or BIDAF,

asr-000186
00:36:29.740 --> 00:36:34.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and the Tripartite Implementation Monitoring Committee, or TMC, remaining.

asr-000187
00:36:34.740 --> 00:36:38.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The MNLF transformation program is at 16% completion

asr-000188
00:36:38.740 --> 00:36:40.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: across the security,

asr-000189
00:36:40.740 --> 00:36:42.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: socioeconomic development, confidence-building,

asr-000190
00:36:42.740 --> 00:36:44.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and healing and reconciliation

asr-000191
00:36:44.740 --> 00:36:47.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: components.

asr-000192
00:36:48.080 --> 00:36:49.680
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Under the peace process with the

asr-000193
00:36:49.680 --> 00:36:54.800
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Cordillera-Bodong Administration-Cordillera People's Liberation Army,

asr-000194
00:36:54.800 --> 00:36:59.440
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: or CBA-CPLA, 91% have been accomplished,

asr-000196
00:36:59.440 --> 00:37:03.000
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: which includes the full decommissioning of the CBA-CPLA,

asr-000197
00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:06.000
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and the integration of its members

asr-000198
00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:08.990
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: into the Armed Forces of the Philippines.

asr-000199
00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:26.510
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Socioeconomic interventions have also been implemented in the majority of identified communities. The implementation of interventions and assistance under the healing and reconciliation and confidence-building components comprise the bulk of the remaining deliverables.

asr-000200
00:37:28.200 --> 00:37:49.700
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: For the peace process with the Revolucionary Partido ng Manggagawa Pilipinas, Revolutionary Proletarian Army Alex Boncayo Brigade, or RPMP-RPA-ABB, 85% of the commitments have been completed, including Kapatiran's disposition of arms and forces, community peace dividends, and social and economic reintegration programs.

asr-000201
00:37:49.700 --> 00:37:53.820
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Key deliberables remain, including the continued development of

asr-000202
00:37:53.980 --> 00:37:59.340
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: settlement sites and the organizational development of Kapatiran chapters.

asr-000203
00:38:01.420 --> 00:38:23.960
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Pursuant to the Local Government Code and Executive Order No. 70, Series of 2018, OPAPRU supports provincial local government units in the local peace engagement and further capacitating them in the development of transformation programs which aim to mainstream CPP-NP-NDF surrenders into the society and enable them to

asr-000204
00:38:23.960 --> 00:38:31.180
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and their families to be resilient from the resurgence the CPP-NP-NDF influence.

asr-000205
00:38:32.020 --> 00:38:36.240
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The program has accomplished 65% of its target provinces.

asr-000206
00:38:38.440 --> 00:38:53.240
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Recapitulating the status of peace agreements, the implementation of peace agreements across the four peace tables have achieved the following percentage completion as shown with the RPMP-RPA-ABB.

asr-000207
00:38:53.960 --> 00:39:02.260
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The peace process as early as September 30, 2026 has already achieved the target 85% completion.

asr-000208
00:39:03.260 --> 00:39:19.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: And by the end of the current year 2026, the targeted achievements would be 72% implemented commitments under the GPH-MILF peace process, 53% for the peace process with the MNLF, including its transformation program,

asr-000209
00:39:19.740 --> 00:39:23.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and 100% completion of the commitments.

asr-000210
00:39:23.960 --> 00:39:34.380
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: For our fiscal year 2025 financial performance, as of December 31, 2025.

asr-000211
00:39:34.380 --> 00:39:45.440
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: We have obligated 97% or 6.9 billion of the total 7.1 billion agency appropriations for fiscal year 2025.

asr-000212
00:39:46.320 --> 00:39:49.800
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: For fiscal year 2026 status of funds.

asr-000213
00:39:49.860 --> 00:39:52.800
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: As of September 30, 2026.

asr-000214
00:39:53.440 --> 00:39:53.920
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: We have.

asr-000215
00:39:53.960 --> 00:40:03.420
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: We have utilized 73% or 6.1 billion pesos of the total 8.3 billion for 2026 agency appropriation.

asr-000216
00:40:04.300 --> 00:40:09.800
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Of this amount, 4.6 billion pesos was obligated for Pomana infrastructure projects

asr-000217
00:40:09.800 --> 00:40:17.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: while the remaining funds supported OPA-PRO regular and ongoing normalization and transformation programs.

asr-000218
00:40:17.720 --> 00:40:26.480
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Anchored on the President's Directive for OPA-PRO to achieve substantial completion of the peace agreements,

asr-000219
00:40:27.120 --> 00:40:33.900
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: our proposal highlights investing in peace, investing in continuous sustainable development.

asr-000220
00:40:33.900 --> 00:40:42.960
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: To accelerate the peace agreements implementation, we must pursue post-conflict reconstruction, rehabilitation, and development.

asr-000221
00:40:43.900 --> 00:40:47.700
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Its implementation suffered significant delays in previous years,

asr-000222
00:40:47.720 --> 00:40:55.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: due to the COVID-19 pandemic, governance, and political transitions, which have put us in a critical catch-up phase.

asr-000223
00:40:57.640 --> 00:41:05.580
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Peace Care Year 2027 is a crucial year to fully fund and fast-track the normalization and transformation programs

asr-000224
00:41:05.580 --> 00:41:13.180
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: as we work toward fulfilling the national governance commitment under the signed peace agreements by 2028.

asr-000225
00:41:15.060 --> 00:41:17.680
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: We must also scale up socioeconomic integrity.

asr-000226
00:41:17.720 --> 00:41:22.400
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: For foreign rebels or combatants, their families and communities,

asr-000227
00:41:23.180 --> 00:41:27.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: to address the root causes of un-conflict, eliminate the triggers for recruitment,

asr-000228
00:41:28.440 --> 00:41:32.240
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and prevent the threats of renewed violence and rebellion.

asr-000229
00:41:32.240 --> 00:41:38.280
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: We are likewise advancing the localization of normalization and transformation implementation

asr-000230
00:41:38.280 --> 00:41:45.100
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: to ensure that interventions are felt where they are needed most,

asr-000231
00:41:45.640 --> 00:41:47.640
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: right on the ground, inside our communities,

asr-000232
00:41:47.720 --> 00:41:48.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and outside our priority communities.

asr-000233
00:41:48.720 --> 00:41:54.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Finally, while our proposed funding is substantial,

asr-000234
00:41:54.720 --> 00:42:01.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: it remains insufficient to address the holistic requirements of sustaining peace across all target areas.

asr-000235
00:42:01.720 --> 00:42:06.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: We will continue to mobilize support from other government agencies,

asr-000236
00:42:06.720 --> 00:42:11.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: as well as local and international development partners to bridge this gap.

asr-000237
00:42:11.720 --> 00:42:17.260
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: However, robust baseline funding for Fiscal Year 2027

asr-000238
00:42:17.720 --> 00:42:24.940
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: from the national budget remains the critical catalyst for leveraging these resources.

asr-000239
00:42:24.940 --> 00:42:28.260
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The budget requests are not mere expenditures,

asr-000240
00:42:28.260 --> 00:42:34.520
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: they are urgent investments in securing a just, sustainable, and lasting peace.

