asr-000464
00:49:35.440 --> 00:49:41.060
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: with 31 institutionalized and 28 peace development centers established.

asr-000465
00:49:42.100 --> 00:49:47.020
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: 29 former rebels' organizations have also become members of the local bodies,

asr-000466
00:49:47.780 --> 00:49:53.320
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: institutionalizing former rebels' meaningful participation in local governance.

asr-000467
00:49:53.320 --> 00:49:59.680
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: These milestones demonstrate that local governments are taking ownership,

asr-000468
00:50:00.760 --> 00:50:06.100
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: former rebels are steadily reintegrating, and communities are moving towards stability.

asr-000469
00:50:06.880 --> 00:50:12.320
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: To sustain and expand these gains, the goal is to ensure that all 59 provinces

asr-000470
00:50:12.900 --> 00:50:19.320
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: achieve ownership of their respective TP plans supported by operational peace and development centers,

asr-000471
00:50:19.320 --> 00:50:23.320
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: while also capacitating 1,000 people.

asr-000472
00:50:23.320 --> 00:50:31.320
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: It is the goal of the 1209th former rebel organization to become self-reliant and productive partners in peace and development.

asr-000473
00:50:33.320 --> 00:50:40.360
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The peace process with the Revolucionaryong Partido ng Manggagawa Pilipinas, Alex Boncayo Brigade,

asr-000474
00:50:40.900 --> 00:50:47.400
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: has made significant strides through the completion of the peace agreement and transformation program.

asr-000475
00:50:47.400 --> 00:50:52.400
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Key accomplishments include the decommissioning of 727,

asr-000476
00:50:53.320 --> 00:50:59.560
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: members, and the provision of 50.4 million in socio-economic assistance.

asr-000477
00:50:59.560 --> 00:51:08.560
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The program has also delivered 105 housing units and site development projects worth 371 million,

asr-000478
00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:15.560
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: while 100 barangays have benefited from sustainable livelihood grants totaling 110 million.

asr-000479
00:51:17.240 --> 00:51:22.560
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Other initiatives implemented include capacity development for women in transformation,

asr-000481
00:51:24.320 --> 00:51:34.240
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and for Kapatiran members in organizational development and social entrepreneurship and enterprise development.

asr-000482
00:51:34.960 --> 00:51:39.020
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Moving forward, the program will focus on the remaining deliverables

asr-000483
00:51:39.020 --> 00:51:41.900
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: to ensure the full completion of its commitments.

asr-000484
00:51:42.740 --> 00:51:50.480
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: These include the completion of 15 settlement sites and 531 remaining housing units,

asr-000488
00:51:50.740 --> 00:52:04.800
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: full transformation of the group into a civilian organization, and the active re-engagement with the Nilo de la Cruz group and strengthening multi-sectoral and local partnership to ensure sustainability.

asr-000489
00:52:08.060 --> 00:52:19.740
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The peace process with the Cordillera-Bodong Administration, Cordillera People's Liberation Army, has significantly advanced the peace agreement and normalization program in the Cordillera.

asr-000490
00:52:19.740 --> 00:52:30.520
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: A total of 550 members were employed as forest guards, while 481 members and their next sub-queen were integrated into the armed forces of the Philippines.

asr-000491
00:52:31.440 --> 00:52:39.140
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Social protection, educational assistance, and livelihood projects were 482 million were also implemented.

asr-000492
00:52:39.860 --> 00:52:49.280
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Peace memorials or peace markers made from decommissioned firearm parts have been installed at historic sites in the Cordillera.

asr-000493
00:52:49.740 --> 00:52:55.080
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: While the DIO program empowered women, youth, and community organizations.

asr-000494
00:52:56.220 --> 00:53:14.420
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: For 2027, the program will complete the remaining 23 community livelihood projects, document stakeholder experiences to memorialize the Cordillera's aspiration to sustain the peace gains through infrastructure projects,

asr-000495
00:53:14.420 --> 00:53:18.820
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: and operationalize the interagency cluster mechanism.

asr-000496
00:53:19.740 --> 00:53:28.860
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: The Cordillera transformation to institutionalized coordination, advancing peace, self-reliance, and regional transformation.

asr-000497
00:53:30.780 --> 00:53:48.200
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: From fiscal year 2024 to 2026, the Payapa at Masanganang Pamayanan or PAMANA program funded 358 socioeconomic development infrastructure projects

asr-000498
00:53:48.200 --> 00:53:49.380
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: across the different regions.

asr-000499
00:53:49.740 --> 00:54:17.660
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: For fiscal year 2027, PAMANA has a proposed allocation of 4.9 billion for infrastructure projects to help improve the condition of geographically isolated, conflict-affected and vulnerable communities in the Bangsamoro and adjacent areas as well as in CPP-NPA-NDF, RPMP-RPA-ABB and Cordillera areas.

asr-000501
00:54:19.740 --> 00:54:39.180
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Of this amount, 1.6 billion is allocated for the MILF peace process, 624 million for the MNLF peace process, 1.5 billion for local conflict transformation, and a total of 1.1 billion is allocated for the RPMP-RPA-ABB and CBA-CPLA peace processes.

asr-000502
00:54:39.180 --> 00:54:49.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: These allocations mainly support the completion of remaining commitments under the respective peace agreements and the sustainment of peace gains.

asr-000503
00:54:49.740 --> 00:55:01.760
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: For 2027 projects, they are still subject for further validation, particularly on implementation, readiness, and compliance with program requirements.

asr-000504
00:55:02.360 --> 00:55:06.820
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Thus, the amounts presented represent allocation at this stage.

asr-000505
00:55:07.840 --> 00:55:17.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: PAMANA will also prioritize the completion of projects funded from fiscal year 2024 to 2026.

asr-000506
00:55:25.760 --> 00:55:44.520
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: With the projected heightened and accelerated implementation of commitments under the signed peace agreements, the provided allocation for OPAPRU is expected to bring us to the following levels of completion by the end of 2027.

asr-000507
00:55:44.520 --> 00:56:00.220
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Our target milestones reflect the government?s commitment to long-term peacebuilding, sustainable development, community empowerment, and the successful reintegration of former rebels and combatants into mainstream society.

asr-000508
00:56:02.060 --> 00:56:18.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: In light of the intensified focus on economic recovery and our shared goal of achieving greater peace, progress, and stability in core and additional priority areas, we humbly seek your full support for

asr-000516
00:56:19.720 --> 00:56:20.920
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: OPAPRU programs.

asr-000517
00:56:21.760 --> 00:56:23.520
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: We earnestly seek your

asr-000518
00:56:23.520 --> 00:56:24.600
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: favorable consideration

asr-000519
00:56:24.600 --> 00:56:27.760
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: for the approval of OPA-PRO's

asr-000520
00:56:27.760 --> 00:56:29.960
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: fiscal year 2027

asr-000521
00:56:29.960 --> 00:56:30.920
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: budget of

asr-000522
00:56:30.920 --> 00:56:33.920
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: 9.3 billion to address

asr-000523
00:56:33.920 --> 00:56:35.440
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: the budget gap for

asr-000524
00:56:35.440 --> 00:56:36.640
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: 2027.

asr-000525
00:56:37.700 --> 00:56:39.360
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: Lastly, as the rationale

asr-000526
00:56:39.360 --> 00:56:40.760
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: behind our proposal

asr-000527
00:56:40.760 --> 00:56:43.860
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: that sustainable development goes on in hand

asr-000528
00:56:43.860 --> 00:56:45.720
OPAPRU Presidential Assistant Wilben M. Mayor: with sustaining the gains of

asr-000529
