Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Asik, well, I'm just sorry to interrupt you.

asr-001694
01:35:29.540 --> 01:35:37.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But I remember during my visit a few months ago, I had a chance to meet, I don't know if it was Governor Midtimbang.

asr-001695
01:35:37.060 --> 01:35:42.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa Maguindanao, the newly created Maguindanao del Norte and Maguindanao del Sur, si Bastura.

asr-001696
01:35:44.260 --> 01:35:45.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Nagkaroon ng issue doon eh.

asr-001697
01:35:45.580 --> 01:35:51.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That there was, I don't know kung plantation yun, na there are about 5,000 workers already there, no?

asr-001698
01:35:51.660 --> 01:35:57.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That parang, for some reason, nagsara. Sayang din yung 5,000 workers.

asr-001699
01:35:58.060 --> 01:36:02.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That's providing employment, hanap buhay po ito para sa mga doon sa conflict areas.

asr-001700
01:36:03.240 --> 01:36:05.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Any update kung ano po nangyari doon?

asr-001701
01:36:05.100 --> 01:36:11.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi nakapanghihinayang, 5,000 planters [unclear] na hindi ko alam bakit.

asr-001702
